  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759154,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 100 Meter Slith: A Commodore 64 Challenge\n\nPrepare for a frantic, pixelated race against the clock in *100 Meter Slith*! This unique Commodore 64 game throws you into a bizarre, subterranean world where you control a constantly-growing worm, tasked with slithering through a series of increasingly challenging tunnels. \n\nThe gameplay is simple yet addictive: use the joystick to guide your worm, consuming pellets to increase its length. But beware! The tunnels are riddled with obstacles – rocks, walls, and even other, smaller worms – that can quickly end your run.  Strategic maneuvering and quick reflexes are essential to avoid collisions and navigate the twisting pathways. \n\nAs your worm grows, so does the difficulty. The tunnels become tighter, the obstacles more frequent, and the pressure mounts to reach the 100-meter mark.  *100 Meter Slith* offers a frantic, arcade-style experience with vibrant graphics and a catchy chiptune soundtrack, perfect for short bursts of addictive gameplay. Can you master the slither and conquer the 100-meter challenge?"
    },
